        1133.86,
        453.54
      ],
      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "We compared PostgreSQL against MongoDB. The argument for a document store is schema flexibility. The argument against, here, is that our hardest requirements are constraint-shaped.\n\nA run must not sit in a state its decisions do not justify. A report version must not be submitted before it was created. One line of SQL each — application code everywhere else.\n\nThe payoff, months later: an end-to-end test started failing intermittently. The CHECK constraint submitted_at >= created_at was refusing rows. The constraint was right — the host clock and the database container clock were 0.44 seconds apart, so records really were dated after they were stored.\n\nWe chose the database that could refuse. It refused something real.",
      "textPreview": "We compared PostgreSQL against MongoDB. The argument for a document store is schema flexibility. The argument against, here, is that our ...",
