      "textLayout": {
        "lineCount": 11,
        "lines": [
          {
            "index": 1,
            "text": "We compared PostgreSQL against MongoDB. The argument for a document store is schema flexibility. The argument against, here, is"
          },
          {
            "index": 2,
            "text": "that our hardest requirements are constraint-shaped."
          },
          {
            "index": 3,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "index": 4,
            "text": "A run must not sit in a state its decisions do not justify. A report version must not be submitted before it was created. One line of SQL"
          },
          {
            "index": 5,
            "text": "each — application code everywhere else."
          },
          {
            "index": 6,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "index": 7,
            "text": "The payoff, months later: an end-to-end test started failing intermittently. The CHECK constraint submitted_at >= created_at was"
          },
          {
            "index": 8,
            "text": "refusing rows. The constraint was right — the host clock and the database container clock were 0.44 seconds apart, so records really"
          },
          {
            "index": 9,
            "text": "were dated after they were stored."
          },
          {
            "index": 10,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "index": 11,
            "text": "We chose the database that could refuse. It refused something real."
          }
        ]
